  "known_quirks": [
    "Racket count-solutions uses for/and, aborting the whole candidate loop on the first dead-end branch: it returns 0 for solvable unique puzzles (hard-17, escargot) and undercounts row1-filled at cap 3 (Racket reports 2). Rust implements the correct capped counting (unique=true, count_solutions_cap2=1, row1-filled cap3=3 above) — a deliberate, documented divergence."
